{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "f4a1c7d3-9b2e-4f68-8e4a-walletsnap0127",
    "name": "Wallet Snapshot Admin API - majdpay (dev)",
    "description": "EMI-6127 (BE - Create Wallet Snapshot Admin Page): two read-only Admin-portal endpoints over the existing wallet-snapshot subsystem (wallet_snapshots / wallet_snapshot_events / wallet_snapshot_verifications). See docs/business-knowledge/EMI-6127-Refined-Ticket.md for the full refinement and gap list, and docs/business-knowledge/Wallet-Snapshot-Pipeline-Architecture.md for the full 13-ticket epic this belongs to.\n\nThe on-demand snapshot job-trigger endpoint (EMI-6115) used to live here as a fourth folder - it has since moved to its own dedicated collection, postman/WalletSnapshotJob-API-majdpay.postman_collection.json, since it lives on a different host with a different auth posture entirely (no auth at all, vs. this collection's bearer token). Use that collection for anything related to triggering a snapshot run.\n\nBase URL: https://gateway-dev.majdpay.com. Both GET routes confirmed LIVE and reachable in dev as of 2026-09-29 (unauthenticated calls answered 401, not 404). Required privilege: ADMIN_GET_WALLET_SNAPSHOTS.\n\nHeaders are an EXACT match to a real captured Admin Portal browser request against gateway-dev.majdpay.com/api/v1/admin/wallet-snapshots (2026-10), including the browser-injected ones (Connection, Origin, Referer, Sec-Fetch-*, User-Agent, sec-ch-ua*) - not just the app-level subset. {{token}} must be a real Bearer JWT for an admin user holding ADMIN_GET_WALLET_SNAPSHOTS - mint one by signing in through the Admin Portal (BusinessTestCases/pageElements/Shared/AdminOtpConfigPage.ts) and pasting the resulting token, since no pure-API admin sign-in contract is confirmed yet (the business-portal /auth/signin + tenantNumber flow returns 401 for admin credentials - it is a separate auth realm). A captured token typically lives ~18 minutes (iat to exp) - paste a fresh one right before running folders 1-2, a stale one will 401 exactly like no token at all. {{deviceFingerPrint}} is left empty by design: the real value is generated client-side per session and itself embeds the current access token, so it cannot be a static committed value - capture a fresh one from a live browser session if a request needs it to pass, or leave it empty.\n\nTwo known defects on the GET endpoints, deliberately encoded as failing assertions below rather than as passing ones (regression tripwires, not smoke tests):\n1. openingBalances/movementBalances (list and detail) put the available balance into the 'current' field and leave 'available' null. closingBalances is unaffected.\n2. detail's validationDetails[].verificationSteps is always null (DTO field name 'verificationSteps' vs entity field 'verifications', no MapStruct mapping between them).\n\nFolder 3 (Negative / Auth) sends every header above EXCEPT Authorization (empty/omitted) and needs no token - it is the part of this collection already confirmed live (401, not 404).",
